{"name":"Eigengrau","hex":"#16161d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eigengrau","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The dark grey colour seen by the eyes in perfect darkness as a result of signals from the optic nerves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eigengrau"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eigengrau","blocks":[{"text":"Eigengrau, also called Eigenlicht, dark light, or brain gray, is the uniform dark gray background color that many people report seeing in the absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/CrumeyFig3.pdf/page1-330px-CrumeyFig3.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eigengrau"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/CrumeyFig3.pdf/page1-500px-CrumeyFig3.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/CrumeyFig3.pdf/page1-1280px-CrumeyFig3.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/CrumeyFig3.pdf/page1-500px-CrumeyFig3.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Threshold increment versus background luminance for various target diameters (in arcmin). Data from tables 4 and 8 of Blackwell (1946), plotted in Crumey (2014). The flat curves at low light indicate Eigengrau.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrumeyFig3.pdf"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Photon-noise.jpg/500px-Photon-noise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Photon-noise.jpg/1280px-Photon-noise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik